    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` assignment for owners, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is the last two digits of the registration date's year.\n\nSince a membership number is purely a function of two fields the owner already carries (`customerCode` and `registrationDate`), I modeled it as a derived, read-only property rather than a stored column \u2014 mirroring how the codebase already handles `initials` (`@Transient` getter on `Person`). This keeps it seed-independent and always consistent with its source fields, and sidesteps an ordering bug: `registrationDate` is defaulted late, in `@PrePersist`, so computing/storing it during `saveOwner` could see a null date.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getMembershipNumber()` that formats `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, returning null until both source fields are present. The formatting logic lives on the domain object next to its other derived accessors.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it from the getter (no mapper changes needed).\n\nNo DB migration, generator, or service wiring was required. `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full build pass.",
